er":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T17:26:41-08:00","id":1498711,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415681-marcus-vitel\u2019s-betrayal?p=1498708#post1498708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Every ST is overly nice some days.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I've been there before, but funny enough, one thing I found out talking to my players friends (I'm almost never a &quot;player&quot;, as I'm ST like 99% of the time) is that they don't like when I take it too easy, they like the challenge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T12:39:19-08:00","id":1498782,"title":"","content":"That always made my eyes roll when game masters were to generous when we could confront old potent monsters and take them out to easily. Going up against a 4-6th generation monster should be very hard and require really good planning and teamwork to pull off and even then it should be with heavy losses.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":27361,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","user":"Lysander","date":". 12-04-2022, 03:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T13:16:00-08:00","id":1498792,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415681-marcus-vitel\u2019s-betrayal?p=1498782#post1498782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That always made my eyes roll when game masters were to generous when we could confront old potent monsters and take them out to easily. Going up against a 4-6th generation monster should be very hard and require really good planning and teamwork to pull off and even then it should be with heavy losses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I kind of think they had the right idea that some NPCs should remain statless.<br /> <br /> Like Cthulhu, if you meet Etrius or Ur-Shulgi, the issue is only how long it takes them to devour your soul.<br /> <br /> My biggest issue with 5th Edition would be better solved if Critias, Helena, and Mithras (rebooted) had no stat blocks. Methusalehs being &quot;They have learned more things than any V5 PC will ever be able to deal with.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T19:09:39-08:00","id":1498810,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415681-marcus-vitel\u2019s-betrayal?p=1498792#post1498792\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, I kind of think they had the right idea that some NPCs should remain statless.<br /> <br /> Like Cthulhu, if you meet Etrius or Ur-Shulgi, the issue is only how long it takes them to devour your soul.<br /> <br /> My biggest issue with 5th Edition would be better solved if Critias, Helena, and Mithras (rebooted) had no stat blocks. Methusalehs being &quot;They have learned more things than any V5 PC will ever be able to deal with.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In fact V5 would have avoided a great deal of criticism if it had opted for going this way. If they had presented powers up to only level 5, but then left blood gods like Mithras or even Lord Camden statless, just mentioning something like &quot;They have learned more things than the PCs are going to be able to deal with&quot; to go along the lines you used, it would be much more interesting. Unfortunately they instead chose to give Mithras yet another terrible character sheet (one could argue that it's still perhaps not as bad as the 1st edition one as at least they remembered to give him Auspex and blood magic, while they forgot to even give him that in &quot;A World of Darkness&quot;. I mean come on, his character sheet was worse than his child Cretheus, likely because Cret's was made later...) that could still be somewhat easily deposed of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12348-herr-meister","name":"Herr Meister","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12348_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-06T11:50:48-08:00","id":1498981,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The smiling gun-knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415681-marcus-vitel\u2019s-betrayal?p=1498707#post1498707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> there no way that happened the dice should have been in the Lupines side no matter how badly they rolled.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, way. They rolled very very badly and the player (Gangrel) rerolled, rerolled and rerolled. Pure luck, but still. And remember, either you roll or side with one of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Warrior of the Rainbow<br /> Saint among the sinners<br /> Pure among the dirt<br /> Loser among winners","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13141-nail-eater","name":"Nail Eater","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"577"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-06T12:41:44-08:00","id":1498985,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415681-marcus-vitel\u2019s-betrayal?p=1415688#post1415688\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Marcus Vitel is a 2000 year old Methuselah who predates both sects. He was also never a member of the Sabbat and hiding his identity from the Camarilla. He was giving the Sabbat information on the Crusade as part of a larger Jyhad that undoubtedly would have put him back on the throne (except Vykos never intended to do it and Marcus knew that Vykos didn't).<br /> <br /> It's never spelled out but Marcus was sabotaging the Camarilla resistance for his own benefit and to make himself more important.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <b>Nearly</b> 2000 years old Methuselah - and that without discounting about two centuries of torpor where Washington grew while he napped - who predates both sects. Damn, Helena and Menele were already Methuselahs before Sejanus was born - he's fine but no Mithras, even Cretheus is older than him by almost half a millenium! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> All of that said, his ties to the Sabbat were a little deeper than people seem to give credit. Writers themselves seem to have mostly forgotten/ignored one of the leading pack leaders was a 700+ years 7th gen Tzimisce who was in cahoots with him all along. That guy should have been some problem to Vykos, even without into the sheer ridiculousness of the whole &quot;Sabbat takes over Washington for a time&quot; scenario in the first place.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Now, about Vitel's fight with Theo Bell &amp; co, i'd say there's much &quot;star power flak&quot; at play in the discussion. Vitel has some good stats and variety of tricks but he's no bonecrushing blood god of war, he's far more manipulator and trickster than fighter while Bell, though not the most ultimately optimized character ever (what everybody would diss him as &quot;haxx&quot; for instead if he were, might be said) is far from bad for someone in the 1-5 range.<br /> <br /> If he's already on close combat range and with some agravated inducing weaponry (like Dragonsbreath rounds, that are cited) at hand, things become close to balanced - the most detestable scenario ever for someone like Vitel - add to the mix Christoff that, game events exageration or not, might be Bell's near equal or even better plus have a magic sword of mysterious powers and it only gets worse.<br /> <br /> Considering there were also a number of less notable anarchs, allies and ghouls involved in the scene and our dearest Lasombra bastard would have to be <i>suicidally </i>stupid <b>not </b>to bolt the first chance he got (something he's immensely better equiped for, might be said), with his cover already blown to smitherens to boot.<br /> <br /> So, i'd say i'm quite fine with Vitel actually faking his destruction in that encounter as of BJD, exactly because he's a slippery bastard with the kind of powerset to <b>not </b>be one-shot into final death <b>and </b>pull off such a stunt of misdirection, but is nowhere near the engine of destruction that some of the fanbase seems to think of him as.<br /> <br /> (what is kind of ironic, considering in my own Milwaukee/BJD chronicle Vitel's participation and cameos were pretty much replaced with Critias and his secret Atlantean blood cult)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 12-11-2022, 10:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-06T22:24:09-08:00","id":1499032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1415681-marcus-vitel\u2019s-betrayal?p=1498782#post1498782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That always made my eyes roll when game masters were to generous when we could confront old potent monsters and take them out to easily. Going up against a 4-6th generation monster should be very hard and require really good planning and teamwork to pull off and even then it should be with heavy losses.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember, the dice can be cruel mistresses. I was in a game where the storyteller used various figures from the Red List in our campaign. One member of the group ended up in the sewers alone facing off against Enkidu, and we expected him to be making a new character sheet very quickly. Cue the storyteller rolling a botch on Enkidu's first action with <b>seven</b> 1s left after all successes were negated.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-11T10:12:16-08:00","id":1499388,"title":"","content":"Funny how the dice gods can be so fickle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}